Today is Friday evening.
I take my bicycle out.
I want to buy some Indian spices for the weekend's cooking.
There is a lot of traffic on the street.
But now I ride the bicycle easily.
After the rain, the streets glisten.
I move through the crowd with ease.
I stop in front of a shop near my house.
The shopkeeper sees me and smiles.
I say to him, 'Hello sir, do you have cardamom and cumin?'
He answers, 'Yes madam, we have all the fresh spices here.'
I say, 'Then please give me fifty grams of cumin and twenty grams of cardamom.'
And also, 'Please give me one bottle of turmeric.'
That shopkeeper puts all those things into one packet.
He gives me that packet and the receipt.
I look at the receipt and give him the rupees.
I place that packet in the bicycle's basket.
I am very excited for tomorrow's cooking.
Then I happily ride my bicycle back home.
